From: juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:10:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] kernel: XamLoaderLaunchTitle keeps its launch path in a
 string

The launch path was a string_view of the guest's string, then of a
joined path: a temporary that ends with its statement, so the view
outlived the memory it pointed at. GRAW's Steam Deck run found the
requested path holding glibc's free-list pointers when its campaign
launched the front end. Copy it into a std::string. From
graw360-recomp (tools/patches/rexglue-bd833a2-launch-title-path.patch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp b/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp
index 1fda053..424d02e 100644
--- a/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/xam/xam_info.cpp
@@ -268,7 +268,8 @@ void XamLoaderLaunchTitle_entry(mapped_string raw_name_ptr, u32 flags) {
 
   // Translate the launch path to a full path.
   if (raw_name_ptr) {
-    auto path = raw_name_ptr.value();
+    // A copy: the joined path below is a temporary that a string_view would outlive.
+    std::string path(raw_name_ptr.value());
     if (path.empty()) {
       loader_data.launch_path = "game:\\default.xex";
     } else {
-- 
